==================================================
10. CODE REPAIR ENGINE
==================================================

Implement a controlled repair workflow.

Step 1:
Reproduce or identify the problem.

Step 2:
Collect actual error messages, logs, source locations, and relevant
configuration.

Step 3:
Determine the most likely root cause.

Step 4:
Separate confirmed causes from hypotheses.

Step 5:
Inspect affected dependencies and callers.

Step 6:
Prepare one or more candidate patches.

Step 7:
Show the exact file changes.

Step 8:
Run appropriate static checks.

Step 9:
Run relevant tests in the isolated environment.

Step 10:
Compare results against the original baseline.

Step 11:
Check for regressions.

Step 12:
Present the proposed patch and evidence for approval.

Step 13:
Apply the patch to the approved working branch.

Step 14:
Record the resulting version and test status.

Never hide a failing test merely because a different test passed.

Never delete a test just to make a build appear successful.

Never weaken security controls to silence a scanner without explicit
technical justification and review.

When a repair cannot be verified, mark it NOT VERIFIED.

When the required compiler, SDK, device, dependency, or service is
unavailable, mark the operation BLOCKED and identify the missing
capability.

